{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "label": "Behaviors namespace", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A collection of combinators that build Behavior<T> values, so actors compose as values rather than classes; an actor lifetime is just a sequence of behaviors, each handler returning the next."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior", "label": "Behavior<T>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Describes what the actor does on the next message and which behavior it adopts afterwards \u2014 transitions are explicit returns, state lives in closure parameters, there is no `this`."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receive", "label": "Behaviors.receive", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receivemessage", "label": "Behaviors.receiveMessage", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shortcut for the common case where the context is not needed; equivalent to Behaviors.receive((_context, message) => ...)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receivewithsignal", "label": "Behaviors.receiveWithSignal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The typed-DSL equivalent of overriding postStop/preRestart and handling Terminated messages in the untyped form."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_setup", "label": "Behaviors.setup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs once at actor start so one-time initialization (spawning children, capturing context.self, opening connections) can be closed over by the receive handler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_withtimers", "label": "Behaviors.withTimers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Captures the TimerScheduler in a closure so the receive handler reaches it without going through context.timers on every message."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_withstash", "label": "Behaviors.withStash", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two deliberate differences from the context form: capacity is per behavior rather than one default for the whole actor, and stash(message) takes the message explicitly so it need not be the one being handled \u2014 which is why a dead letter minted from this buffer carries no original sender."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_supervise", "label": "Behaviors.supervise(...).onFailure(...)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The restart tally belongs to the supervise wrapper rather than to the strategy, so one strategy value handed to several behaviors gives each its own allowance."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_intercept", "label": "Behaviors.intercept", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Typed T -> T: an interceptor observes, transforms, or drops but never changes the actor message type. It cannot collapse away like the other decorators because it has to be present on the next message too."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_monitor", "label": "Behaviors.monitor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Forward-then-deliver is deliberate: the monitor sees a message even if handling it crashes the actor, which is the case you most want the trace for. Delivery is fire-and-forget and its failures are swallowed so a broken tap cannot take the actor down."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_logmessages", "label": "Behaviors.logMessages", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only debug/info levels are offered \u2014 logging every message is a diagnostic and reporting it at warn/error would poison the signal an operator filters on. A throwing formatter falls back to the built-in line, and the line is only built when the logger would emit it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_same", "label": "Behaviors.same (sentinel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A singleton value the runtime recognizes and shortcuts, so it is cheaper than returning a freshly-constructed receive value."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_stopped", "label": "Behaviors.stopped (sentinel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The only way out of a supervise or intercept scope; it also leaves a signal handler installed, because a post-stop handler that stopped working the moment the actor stopped would be useless."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_unhandled", "label": "Behaviors.unhandled (sentinel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_empty", "label": "Behaviors.empty (sentinel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_ignore", "label": "Behaviors.ignore (sentinel)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_typedactorcontext", "label": "TypedActorContext<T>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_setdisplayname", "label": "context.setDisplayName", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every Behavior runs inside the same TypedActor class, so there is no subclass on which to override Actor.displayName(); without it a whole tree of typed actors reports TypedActor and the DevTools tree says nothing about which is which."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_timerscheduler", "label": "TimerScheduler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_oneforonestrategy", "label": "OneForOneStrategy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_directive_escalate", "label": "Directive.Escalate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_supervision_scope", "label": "Supervision scope outlives the subtree", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The wrapper contributes its side effect once and the framework remembers the strategy, so a behavior the wrapped one transitions to is still supervised even though the wrapper is nowhere in the returned value. Same rule intercept follows."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_supervision_scope_nesting", "label": "Nested supervision scopes layer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two wrappers make two scopes and the innermost decides first; Escalate and a spent restart budget hand the same error to the next scope out. A restart decided by an outer scope re-resolves its own child and so rebuilds the inner scopes with a full allowance."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_restart_budget", "label": "Restart budget (maxRetries / withinTimeRangeMs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bounds how often Restart may fire in a sliding window; exhausting it escalates to the actor cell rather than looping in place. maxRetries: -1 is unlimited (the hand-built default), 0 never restarts."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_signal_handler_scoping", "label": "Signal handlers are scoped to the declaring behavior", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The handler belongs to the behavior, not the actor: transitioning to a plain receive that declares no onSignal unregisters it, so a state machine must re-declare onSignal in every state that needs post-stop cleanup or a Terminated signal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "label": "Decorator composition order (outside-in)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrappers compose outside-in and the order is directly observable for interceptors: each wrapper decides whether the next one downwards sees the message at all. supervise outermost is almost always the right nesting."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_decorator_collapse", "label": "Decorators collapse, interceptors persist", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Non-interceptor decorators are resolved away once the actor starts \u2014 they contribute their side effect and collapse into the behavior they produced. Collapsing is not expiring: a supervise scope outlives the value that installed it; only the wrapper node is gone."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_spawntypedanonymous", "label": "system.spawnTypedAnonymous", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_dead_letters", "label": "Dead letters for unhandled and orphaned stash", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "unstashAll puts buffered messages back at the FRONT of the mailbox so they precede anything that arrived while the stash filled; whatever is still parked at stop or restart goes to dead letters rather than vanishing."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receive", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receive", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receivemessage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receivemessage", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receivewithsignal", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_receivewithsignal", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_setup", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_setup", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behavior", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_withtimers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_withtimers", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_withstash", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_withstash", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_supervise", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_supervise", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_intercept", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_intercept", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_monitor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_monitor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_logmessages", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_logmessages", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_composition_order", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_same", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/typed/behaviors.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_typed_behaviors_behaviors", "target": "docs_sr